The class `SafeCompletableObserver` is a thin delegating wrapper that adds defensive try/catch logic around downstream calls. Its behavior is deterministic and its performance impact is negligible compared to the actual reactive stream processing. Benchmarking such a small, exception‑handling wrapper with JMH would not provide meaningful insights, as any measured overhead would be dominated by the downstream observer or the surrounding RxJava infrastructure rather than the wrapper itself. Therefore, a JMH benchmark is unnecessary.